Hi there,

I started Deliri Inc - a small tech start-up located in somebody's basement=
. We spend a lot of time thinking up strange things, like what a bastard ch=
ild of a one-night-stand between YouTube and Wikipedia would look like. We =
just wanted to invite you to take a look at said child, and our attempt at =
a solution for the oldest problem humanity has been plagued with: cross-lan=
guage communication.

Our site (SiLo) attempts to organize and cross link 880 Languages. What lan=
guages, you ask? The usual suspects, plus loads of dialects, sign languages=
, and a few friends from outer space (Klingon, Vulcan, etc.).  This list wo=
uldn't be complete without Lojban and we think this is a perfect place for =
your community to spread the awareness about the language as well as create=
 a digital archive of it for study


________________________________


We believe that those who are not original can't lead, in which case they m=
ight as well forget about it, so here's how our approach is different from =
Google's and just about anyone else out there:

* Context- and grammar-sensitive translations
* Native speakers with proper pronunciation vs. monotonized robot voices
* Support for different dialects
* VIDEO!
* User-generated content
* A suggestion list of related phrases (helpful for learning a language)
* Community-building features
* Soon-to-be implemented moderation to weed out poor contributions
* Eventually on mobile phones/tablets

________________________________


HOW TO USE:

Go to: www.delirisilo.com<http://www.delirisilo.com/> |OR| www.deliri.com/s=
ilo<http://www.deliri.com/silo>

Try searching for "What's your name?"   from English to Lojban.

Search between languages - for example - "O=F9 est la salle de bain?" from =
French to Persian.

Or if you're just looking for a quick demonstration: scroll down to the bot=
tom of the search page and click on any of the latest additions to see how =
it works.


________________________________


The site is ideally viewed using Google Chrome on a Mac or a PC, but any mo=
dern browser should suffice. Mobile/Tablet access is disabled.

The product is still in Beta, which means you may run into the occasional b=
ug or odd behaviour. Refreshing the browser and/or clearing the cache usual=
ly clears up most issues. Know that we're working to fix the problems you'r=
e noticing (and many more you probably won't).

Enjoy your Deliri experience and we look forward to your feedback (good or =
bad).

Thanks in advance for your time and efforts.



